{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-26_ex991-earningsreleaseq32026.htm, sha256 218669fdb1adf3f2bcfe937b6575f5d073366b63618bda08815ffe1f7c15d6eb.\nEX-99.1 2 ex991-earningsreleaseq32026.htm EX-99.1 Ex 99.1 - Earnings Release\nJETBLUE ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2026 RESULTS Airline delivered 18.4% RASM growth; recaptured approximately 87% of higher fuel costs Fort Lauderdale RASM increased nearly 15% on more than 65% capacity growth JetBlue expects 1\u20132 points of 4Q year-over-year operating margin expansion\nNEW YORK (October 26, 2026) - JetBlue Airways Corporation (NASDAQ: JBLU) today reported its financial results for the third quarter of 2026. \"I'm very encouraged by the progress we made in the third quarter,\" said Joanna Geraghty, JetBlue's chief executive officer. \"Resilient demand and strong yields drove revenue well ahead of our initial expectations, allowing us to recapture more of the increase in fuel costs than we initially expected. That momentum has carried into the fourth quarter, and Fort Lauderdale continues to deliver exceptional results even as we significantly grow capacity.\"\n\"We delivered year-over-year adjusted operating margin improvement in the third quarter and expect further expansion in the fourth quarter even with higher fuel prices. Together with continued JetForward execution, this reinforces our confidence in achieving sustained operating profitability in 2027 and delivering at least $1 EPS and positive free cash flow in 2028.\"\nStrong revenue momentum driven by higher yields and resilient demand in 3Q26 \u2022Higher yields, supported by improved revenue management technology, drove the majority of third-quarter revenue outperformance. Both premium and Main achieved double-digit RASM growth and demand remained resilient across peak and off-peak travel periods despite higher fuel. \u2022Revenue strength has extended beyond the peak summer season and into the fourth quarter, with continued revenue improvement expected despite a more challenging year-over-year comparison.\nGrowth in Fort Lauderdale strengthens JetBlue's competitive position \u2022Continued expansion with 15 new destinations and increased frequencies strengthening local schedules and connecting itineraries. Peak daily departures planned to exceed 150 this winter, up 39% year-over-year. JetBlue's fourth quarter seat share expected to reach approximately 37%, up 14 points year-over-year. \u2022Co-brand credit card acquisitions in Broward County increased 55% year-over-year in the third quarter.\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Improving margins and healthy liquidity support bridge to at least $1 EPS target \u2022Underlying unit cost performance excluding fuel remained within initial expectations, excluding approximately four points of disruption-related pressure in the third quarter. \u2022Expect a meaningful step-down in fourth-quarter unit-cost growth excluding fuel, alongside continued revenue strength, to support further margin expansion heading into 2027. \u2022Ended the third quarter with $2.2 billion of liquidity, including a $600 million undrawn credit facility, with an additional $250 million of aircraft-backed financing expected to fund in the fourth quarter subject to customary funding mechanics. \u2022Expanded unencumbered asset base to ~$7 billion, including $2.8 billion in aircraft and engines following updated fleet appraisals and aircraft deliveries paid with cash, providing additional financing flexibility.\nThird Quarter 2026 Financial Results \u2022Third quarter 2026 system capacity increased 2.3% year-over-year, within our revised guidance range (1) of 1.5% to 3.5%. \u2022Operating revenue of $2.8 billion for the third quarter of 2026, an increase of 21.1% year-over-year. \u2022Operating revenue per available seat mile (\"RASM\") increased 18.4% year-over-year, materially exceeding initial expectations and in line with our revised guidance range. \u2022Operating expense per available seat mile (\"CASM\") for the third quarter of 2026 increased 19.4% year-over-year, largely driven by higher fuel prices. - 1 -\n\u2022Operating expense per available seat mile, excluding fuel, other non-airline operating expenses, and special items (\"CASM ex-Fuel\") (2) for the third quarter of 2026 increased 7.0% year-over-year, consistent with the revised guidance. \u2022Average fuel price in the third quarter of 2026 was $3.91 per gallon, 57% higher compared to the prior year period. \u2022Capital expenditures, including predelivery deposits, totaled $189 million (3) in the third quarter, below the revised guidance of approximately $275 million, primarily reflecting the timing of one aircraft delivery and LGA slot payments shifting into the fourth quarter.\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "Third Quarter 2026 Commercial and Financial Highlights \u2022Completed the transition to an upgraded revenue management system, delivering early benefits ahead of expectations through improved forecast accuracy and optimization of Mint\u00ae and connecting itineraries. \u2022Realized loyalty revenue growth of 20% year-over-year in the third quarter, alongside double-digit growth in co-brand spending and more than eightfold growth in Premier Card acquisitions following the card refresh. Opened BlueHouse\u2122 Boston to further enhance the premium customer experience. \u2022Drove TrueBlue's member engagement through Blue Sky, with members redeeming more than 1.1 billion points on United flights since the partnership launched. \u2022Paisly delivered its strongest financial results ever in the third quarter. MileagePlus Travel rental car bookings have outpaced United's previous provider since launch and additional travel offerings are planned throughout 2026 and in the first half of 2027. \u2022Launched sales for BlueFirst\u2122, JetBlue's new domestic first-class experience, across more than 30 routes, with initial service beginning December 8 between Boston and Fort Lauderdale and additional routes launching in phases.\nOutlook \"Our strong revenue performance is encouraging, and we see meaningful runway for further growth as our commercial initiatives continue to mature,\" said Marty St. George, JetBlue's president. \"We're already seeing benefits from enhanced revenue management and growing loyalty engagement, while BlueFirst and our expanding travel offerings represent significant opportunities still ahead. Combined with disciplined capacity deployment, we believe these initiatives position us to build on our revenue momentum into 2027 and beyond.\"\n\"We expect further margin expansion in the fourth quarter despite fuel prices forecasted to be 85% higher than in the same period last year. This is a testament to the compounding benefits of our JetForward strategy, which is improving our revenues and costs as we head into 2027,\" said Ursula Hurley, JetBlue's chief financial officer. \"Importantly, we believe we have the liquidity and financing options to create a strong bridge to at least $1 EPS and positive free cash flow in 2028. We remain focused on disciplined cost execution and capital management as we work toward sustained profitability and positive free cash flow.\"\nFourth Quarter and Full Year 2026 Outlook Estimated 4Q 2026 Estimated FY 2026\nAvailable Seat Miles (\"ASMs\") Year-Over-Year 3.0% - 4.0% 1.5% - 2.5%\nRASM Year-Over-Year 18.0% - 22.0% 13.5% - 14.5%\nCASM Ex-Fuel (2) Year-Over-Year (1.0%) - 1.0% 3.5% - 4.5%\nFuel Price per Gallon (4) $4.64 $3.95\nAdjusted Operating Margin (2) - (4.5%) - (6.5%)\nInterest Expense - ~$590 million\nCapital Expenditures ~$300 million ~$850 million (3)\n- 2 -\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "Earnings Call Details JetBlue will hold a conference call to discuss its quarterly earnings tomorrow, October 27, 2026 at 10:00 a.m. Eastern Time. A live broadcast of the conference call will also be available via the internet at http://investor.jetblue.com. The webcast replay and presentation materials will be archived on the airline's website for at least 30 days. For further details, see the third quarter 2026 Earnings Presentation available via the internet at http://investor.jetblue.com. About JetBlue JetBlue is New York's Hometown Airline\u00ae, and a leading carrier in Boston, Fort Lauderdale-Hollywood, Los Angeles, Orlando and San Juan. JetBlue, known for its low fares and great service, carries customers to more than 100 destinations throughout the United States, Latin America, the Caribbean, Canada and Europe. For more information and the best fares, visit jetblue.com. Notes Our estimated effective tax rate is ~6% for the full year 2026, primarily reflecting a non-cash impact from a valuation allowance included in our forecasted annual effective tax rate.\n(1)Revised guidance as of September 10, 2026. (2)Non-GAAP financial measure; Note A provides a reconciliation of each non-GAAP financial measure used in this release to the most directly comparable GAAP financial measure and explains the reasons management believes that presentation of these non-GAAP financial measures provides useful information to investors regarding JetBlue's financial condition and results of operations. In addition, refer to Note A for further details on non-GAAP forward-looking information. (3)Capital expenditures exclude one Airbus A321neo XLR, which JetBlue expects to sell. (4)Fuel price estimate utilizes the forward Brent crude curve and the forward Brent crude to jet crack spread as of October 16, 2026 to calculate fuel price. Includes fuel taxes and other fuel fees.\n- 3 -\n"}
